From e3b7d74ec4b1166db7aebcf8b35e77d6e504eac2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chatgptyukkuri <chatgptyukkuri@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:22:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] dcomp: Implement devices, targets and visuals, and
 compose swapchains in software.

This is the part of DirectComposition that Chromium uses to show its
output: DCompositionCreateDevice3(), CreateTargetForHwnd(), CreateVisual(),
SetRoot(), SetContent() with a swapchain from CreateSwapChainForComposition(),
offsets, clips and Commit(). With it, WebView2 doesn't need to be told that
it runs on Windows 8 (bug 58921).

Commit() and every present of a swapchain in a committed tree compose the
target window's tree into a bitmap and draw it into the window, or hand it
to UpdateLayeredWindow() for a top-level layered window that isn't driven by
SetLayeredWindowAttributes(). Only translations are applied; scales,
rotations, opacity and effects aren't, and IDCompositionSurface isn't
implemented.

Changes to the tree are visible before Commit() if the swapchain presents
in between.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkAyMz3ChWUcwV1bWoNa1Z
